comments.body:
@ironbelly this looks like a good fit for something else we found while reading the code. Please correct us if we have misread.

Nothing today tells the standing coordinator that a watcher claim has finished. The claim runs in its own short-lived session, and the coordinator's duties name the files to read, but not when to look. Also, the contract says a finished agent's `result.md` is noticed through `/sc:sweep`, but the sweep code does not read that file.

Could the model-free scheduled task in this issue also (a) list claims the coordinator has not adopted yet, and (b) notice new `result.md` files, and wake the coordinator for those? If you would rather keep this issue as it is, we can file a separate one and link it here.
